def tbf_leaders_turnovers(
    season: int,
    competition: Optional[str] = "bsl",
    *,
    return_parsed: bool = True,
    return_as_pandas: bool = False,
    **kwargs,
) -> Union[pl.DataFrame, pd.DataFrame, Dict]:
    """Season leaders in turnovers: the server's top 20 by season total and by per-game average.

    Endpoint: ``GET https://miniappapi.tbf.org.tr/webapi-service/api/Player/get-top-kaybi-leaders``
    Example URL: https://miniappapi.tbf.org.tr/webapi-service/api/Player/get-top-kaybi-leaders?season=2027&competition=bsl

    Args:
        season: Required. Season END year (2027 = the 2026-2027 season). TBF keys a league-season by internal season and activity ids; ``tbf_runtime`` reads them from the league's season list by the END year of the label. A year the list lacks raises NoDataError.
        competition: TBF league: bsl (Basketbol Super Ligi), tbl (second tier) or kbsl (women's Super Ligi). The top flight was named TBL until 2007-08 and is listed under bsl.
        return_parsed: parse the payload through parse_tbf_leaders -> polars DataFrame (default True). Pass return_parsed=False for the raw body (``dict``): the TBF envelope ``{data, isSuccess, message, problemDetails}`` with personal fields redacted, plus ``_request`` (the season, competition, game and team ids the runtime resolved).
        return_as_pandas: with return_parsed, return a pandas DataFrame instead of polars.
        **kwargs: Forwarded to the underlying HTTP getter.

    Returns:
        A polars/pandas DataFrame by default; the raw body (``dict``): the TBF envelope ``{data, isSuccess, message, problemDetails}`` with personal fields redacted, plus ``_request`` (the season, competition, game and team ids the runtime resolved) when ``return_parsed=False``.

    Raises:
        NoDataError: The host answered 404 -- the requested resource does not exist. TBF has nothing for the request (an unknown game or player, a season the league list lacks, an empty list, a finished game before 2025-26 asked for play-by-play or shots).
        AssetFetchError: The fetch failed (a non-2xx answer or a connection failure after retries, e.g. 401/403/429/5xx, or an empty or unreadable 200 body) -- the answer is unknown, not empty. The fetch failed or the answer is not the one asked for (an unfinished game, a body for another game, season, league or team, an error envelope, a redirect, a partial page or a changed capped list).
        ValueError: The host answered 400 / 422 -- the request is wrong; retrying cannot help.

    Example:
        Quick start::

            from sportsdataverse.basketball.tbf import tbf_leaders_turnovers
            tbf_leaders_turnovers(competition='bsl', season=2027)

        See Also:
            * `TBF`_ - the Turkish Basketball Federation whose app backend these wrappers read
            * `wehoop`_ - SportsDataverse women's basketball (R)
            * `hoopR`_ - SportsDataverse men's basketball (R)

        .. _TBF: https://www.tbf.org.tr
        .. _wehoop: https://wehoop.sportsdataverse.org
        .. _hoopR: https://hoopR.sportsdataverse.org

    Notes:
        * Official TBF app API, unofficial for SportsDataverse: the backend of the Turkish Basketball Federation's mobile app (miniappapi.tbf.org.tr), which serves BSL, TBL, KBSL and the other TBF leagues. It needs no key; robots.txt answers 404 on the host, and ``tbf_runtime`` spaces requests at least 1 s apart. SportsDataverse has not ruled on TBF's terms, so payloads are not redistributed as release assets. The vendor's origin hosts (nikayazilim.com) serve the same data without Cloudflare but are deliberately not used, redirects are never followed, and www.tbf.org.tr's interactive Turnstile is neither used nor automated.
        * Coverage: season and competition are parameters (``bsl`` Basketbol Super Ligi, back to 1966-67 in the league list; ``tbl`` second tier; ``kbsl`` women, both from 2015-16). Game wrappers serve FINISHED games only (an unfinished game raises AssetFetchError). Box scores exist from 2006-07 (no starters flagged that season); play-by-play and shots from 2025-26 only, an earlier finished game raises NoDataError. Every game carries a Genius LiveStats id (``genius_id``, joins the ``genius`` family) from 2018-19 on some seasons and on every game of 2025-26 and later. Birth dates, contact details, photos and logos are dropped. Names and category labels are Turkish; the column descriptions give the English gloss.
    """
    if competition not in ("bsl", "tbl", "kbsl"):
        raise ValueError(f"competition must be one of ('bsl', 'tbl', 'kbsl'); got {competition!r}")
    _caller_params = kwargs.pop("params", None) or {}
    _params = {
        "season": season,
        "competition": competition,
    }
    _params.update(_caller_params)
    raw = _get(
        "https://miniappapi.tbf.org.tr/webapi-service/api/Player/get-top-kaybi-leaders",
        params=_params,
        **kwargs,
    )
    if return_parsed:
        return parse_tbf_leaders(raw, return_as_pandas=return_as_pandas, columns=_PARSER_COLUMNS["leaders_turnovers"])
    return raw


